<title>SRI LANKA: Sri Lanka 1996 fertiliser imports at 447,039T.</title>
<headline>Sri Lanka 1996 fertiliser imports at 447,039T.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lanka imported 447,039 tonnes of fertiliser in 1996, down from 525,651 tonnes in 1995, Agriculture Minister D.M. Jayaratne told parliament.</p>
<p>The government spent 1.5 billion rupees on subsidising fertiliser imports to allow importers to sell the commodity, mostly urea, at a lower price, Jayaratne was quoted as saying in parliament papers made available to Reuters on Friday. ($1=58.68 rupees)</p>
</text>
